{"questions":[{"question_id":"1l23ietzh","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2012 Paper 1 Offline","year":2012,"examDate":2012,"subject":"chemistry","chapter":"aldehydes-ketones-and-carboxylic-acids","chapterGroup":"organic-chemistry","topic":"preparation-properties-and-uses-of-carboxylic-acids","type":"mcq","marks":3,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"pthe-carboxyl-functional-group--cooh-is-present-in-jee-advanced-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-edt0whhoqyhzpz1z","content":"<p>The carboxyl functional group (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>COOH) is present in</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"picric acid"},{"identifier":"B","content":"barbituric acid"},{"identifier":"C","content":"ascorbic acid"},{"identifier":"D","content":"aspirin"}],"correct_options":["D"],"explanation":"<p>The structures of the given compounds are as follows. Only aspirin has <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>COOH group.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l254brvd/0baba6db-d7cd-4a38-aba4-42caf720f184/